    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0320" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg270"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your note
                    of the 6th instant, inclosing copies of the President’s proclamation of the 13th
                    ultimo, fixing March 1, 1895, as the date on which the laws of the United
                    States, therein mentioned and relating to the new regulations for preventing
                    collisions at sea, are to take effect.</p>
                <p>I did not fail to transmit to my Government a copy of that communication,
                    together with copies of the proclamation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
